.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-identity-export 1  "export 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-identity\-export \- Print this device\*(Aqs certificate as PEM, never its private key (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0013). Without `\-\-out`, the PEM is the only thing this command writes to stdout, so it pipes directly into `qsh trust add \-\-cert\-file \-` on another host
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh identity export\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print this device\*(Aqs certificate as PEM, never its private key (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0013). Without `\-\-out`, the PEM is the only thing this command writes to stdout, so it pipes directly into `qsh trust add \-\-cert\-file \-` on another host
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write the certificate to this path instead of stdout. Refuses to overwrite an existing file
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
